      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Below (2002) marked a fascinating intersection of supernatural horror and submarine warfare, directed by David Twohy and co-written by Darren Aronofsky. The film follows the USS Tiger Shark during WWII, combining claustrophobic tension reminiscent of <a href=\"/movie/387\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"387\">Das Boot</a> (1981) with ghostly encounters that echo <a href=\"/movie/1933\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1933\">The Others</a> (2001). Its innovative approach to underwater horror created a template that influenced later films like <a href=\"/movie/246080\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"246080\">Black Sea</a> (2014) and <a href=\"/movie/443791\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"443791\">Underwater</a> (2020), while its psychological elements drew from classics like <a href=\"/movie/11772\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"11772\">The Haunting</a> (1963)."
      },
