      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The submarine horror subgenre has always provided fertile ground for exploring psychological tension. Below builds on foundations laid by films like <a href=\"/movie/18784\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"18784\">Run Silent, Run Deep</a> (1958) and <a href=\"/movie/1669\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1669\">The Hunt for Red October</a> (1990), but adds supernatural elements that transform the submarine from mere military vessel to haunted house beneath the waves. The confined spaces and pressure of depth create natural tension that Below expertly exploits."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Director David Twohy, who previously helmed <a href=\"/movie/2787\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"2787\">Pitch Black</a> (2000), brings his talent for creating tension in enclosed spaces. The film's sound design deserves special mention, using the submarine's creaks and groans to heighten supernatural dread in ways that influenced later underwater thrillers like <a href=\"/movie/403119\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"403119\">47 Meters Down</a> (2017) and <a href=\"/movie/345940\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"345940\">The Meg</a> (2018). SUBHEAD: Supernatural Elements at Sea"
      },
