      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's ghostly elements draw from a rich tradition of maritime ghost stories, recalling elements of <a href=\"/movie/9645\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9645\">Ghost Ship</a> (2002) and <a href=\"/movie/26466\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"26466\">Triangle</a> (2009). The way Below handles its supernatural reveals shows remarkable restraint, letting tension build naturally through suggestion rather than relying on explicit scares. This approach shares DNA with sophisticated horror films like <a href=\"/movie/10972\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"10972\">Session 9</a> (2001) and <a href=\"/movie/1433\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1433\">The Devil's Backbone</a> (2001)."
      }
